# Build-context ignore file for packages/mu-engine-server/Dockerfile.
#
# Named `Dockerfile.dockerignore` (not the bare `.dockerignore`) deliberately: this Dockerfile's
# build CONTEXT is the mu-core workspace ROOT (../.. from this directory — see the Dockerfile's
# own header comment for why), not this package directory. BuildKit's per-Dockerfile ignore-file
# convention — "<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore", resolved relative to the context root, takes
# precedence over a root-level `.dockerignore` when present" (Docker docs, "Dockerfile-specific
# ignore files") — would let this ignore file live entirely inside packages/mu-engine-server/
# (this task's own owned directory) while still applying to the mu-core-root build context.
#
# VERIFIED NOT ACTIVE IN THIS ENVIRONMENT: that convention is BuildKit-only, and this host's
# Docker has no `buildx` plugin installed (`docker buildx version` -> "unknown command: docker
# buildx"), so `docker build`/`docker compose build` here use the classic (non-BuildKit) builder,
# which reads ONLY a `.dockerignore` at the context root. The actually-functional ignore file for
# this environment is therefore `../../.dockerignore` (mu-core/.dockerignore) — a small,
# necessary exception to this task's own directory-scoped file ownership, documented there with
# the same rationale. This file is kept (a) as the correct mechanism per Docker's own docs, in
# case `buildx` is installed later, and (b) so a reader diffing this directory sees the intended
# design, not just the environment-specific workaround.
#
# Everything below is relative to the mu-core/ context root.

# VCS / editor
.git
.gitignore
**/.DS_Store

# Python bytecode / caches — never needed in the image, `uv sync --no-editable` builds fresh wheels
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# Pre-existing local virtualenvs on the host — never copied in; the builder stage creates its own
**/.venv
**/venv

# Test trees — not needed to build or run the image (they run in CI against source, not the image)
packages/*/tests

# This package's own Docker deliverables that don't need to be in the context twice / aren't
# referenced by any COPY instruction in the Dockerfile
packages/mu-engine-server/docker-compose*.yml
packages/mu-engine-server/Makefile
packages/mu-engine-server/README.md

# Docs / non-build-relevant repo furniture some checkouts may have alongside mu-core/
**/*.md
!packages/mu-contracts/README.md
!packages/mu-engine/README.md
!packages/mu-engine-server/README.md
